494:   /**
495:    * Forks a new execution, detached from the current.
496:    * <p>
497:    * This can be used to launch a one time background job during request processing.
498:    * The forked execution does not inherit anything from the current execution.
499:    * <p>
500:    * Forked executions MUST NOT write to the response or participate in the handler pipeline at all.
501:    * That is, they should not call methods like {@link #next()} or {@link #insert(Handler...)}.
