746:   /**
747:    * Parses the request body into an object.
748:    * <p>
749:    * How to parse the request is determined by the given {@link Parse} object.
750:    * <h5>Parser Resolution</h5>
751:    * <p>
752:    * Parser resolution happens as follows:
753:    * <ol>
754:    * <li>All {@link ratpack.parse.Parser parsers} are retrieved from the context registry (i.e. {@link #getAll(Class) getAll(Parser.class)});</li>
755:    * <li>Found parsers are checked (in order returned by {@code getAll()}) for compatibility with the current request content type and options type;</li>
756:    * <li>If a parser is found that is compatible, its {@link ratpack.parse.Parser#parse(Context, ratpack.http.TypedData, Parse)} method is called;</li>
757:    * <li>If the parser returns {@code null} the next parser will be tried, if it returns a value it will be returned by this method;</li>
758:    * <li>If no compatible parser could be found, a {@link NoSuchParserException} will be thrown.</li>
759:    * </ol>
760:    * <h5>Parser Compatibility</h5>
761:    * <p>
762:    * A parser is compatible if all of the following hold true:
763:    * <ul>
764:    * <li>Its {@link ratpack.parse.Parser#getContentType()} is exactly equal to {@link ratpack.http.MediaType#getType() getRequest().getBody().getContentType().getType()}</li>
765:    * <li>The opts of the given {@code parse} object is an {@code instanceof} its {@link ratpack.parse.Parser#getOptsType()} ()}</li>
766:    * <li>The {@link ratpack.parse.Parser#parse(Context, ratpack.http.TypedData, Parse)} method returns a non null value.</li>
767:    * </ul>
768:    * <p>
769:    * If the request has no declared content type, {@code text/plain} will be assumed.
770:    * <h5>Core Parsers</h5>
771:    * <p>
772:    * Ratpack core provides implicit {@link ratpack.parse.NoOptParserSupport no opt parsers} for the following types and content types:
773:    * <ul>
774:    * <li>{@link ratpack.form.Form}</li>
775:    * <ul>
776:    *   <li>multipart/form-data</li>
777:    *   <li>application/x-www-form-urlencoded</li>
778:    * </ul>
779:    * </ul>
780:    * <h5>Example Usage</h5>
781:    * <pre class="tested">
782:    * import ratpack.handling.Handler;
783:    * import ratpack.handling.Context;
784:    * import ratpack.form.Form;
785:    * import ratpack.parse.Parse;
786:    * import ratpack.parse.NullParseOpts;
787:    *
788:    * public class FormHandler implements Handler {
789:    *   public void handle(Context context) {
790:    *     Form form = context.parse(Parse.of(Form.class));
791:    *     context.render(form.get("someFormParam"));
792:    *   }
793:    * }
794:    * </pre>
795:    * @param parse The specification of how to parse the request
796:    * @param <T> The type of object the request is parsed into
797:    * @param <O> the type of the parse options object
798:    * @return The parsed object
799:    * @throws NoSuchParserException if no suitable parser could be found in the registry
800:    * @throws ParserException if a suitable parser was found, but it threw an exception while parsing
801:    * @see #parse(Class)
802:    * @see #parse(Class, Object)
803:    * @see ratpack.parse.Parser
804:    */
805:   <T, O> T parse(Parse<T, O> parse) throws NoSuchParserException, ParserException;
